From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: skip AN7581 global reset on same-speed relink

Patch 621 added a global PCS digital reset to an7581_pcs_phya_link_up() so
that a speed change inside the same USXGMII interface re-initialises the
RX data path (only link_up() runs in that case, not pcs_config()). It
skips the reset only for the first link_up after bringup, using the
needs_full_init flag, and therefore runs it on every later link_up -
including a plain cable replug at an unchanged speed.

On the XR1710G that reset destroys a freshly negotiated link: after a
replug the MAC reports "Link is Up - 10Gbps/Full" and the link collapses
again 0.5-0.7 s later, then never recovers; the same port carries traffic
for hours when the link comes up right after bringup. Measured on both
10G PHYs (lan2, wan): first plug after boot works, every replug fails.

Only a real speed change needs the data path re-initialised. Track the
speed seen by airoha_pcs_link_up() in the port and skip the global reset
when it is unchanged, keeping the reset for speed changes.

Signed-off-by: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha.h
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha.h
@@ -1698,6 +1698,8 @@
 	struct airoha_pcs_priv *priv;
 	phy_interface_t interface;
 	int index;
+	int speed;
+	bool speed_changed;
 
 	struct phylink_pcs pcs;
 };
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -998,6 +998,13 @@
 	maps = &priv->maps[port->index];
 	data = priv->data;
 
+	/* Remember whether this link-up follows a real speed change: only
+	 * then does the data path need re-initialising. A cable replug at the
+	 * same speed leaves the PCS/rate-adapt configuration untouched.
+	 */
+	port->speed_changed = port->speed != speed;
+	port->speed = speed;
+
 	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED &&
 	    interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII) {
 		regmap_update_bits(maps->hsgmii_rate_adp,
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -3471,6 +3471,20 @@
 			return;
 		}
 
+		/* The global digital reset below is required when the speed
+		 * changes but it must not run on a plain cable replug: on the
+		 * XR1710G it tears down the just-negotiated in-band link about
+		 * half a second after it comes up, so the port never carries
+		 * traffic again until the netdev is bounced. The same reset
+		 * right after bringup is harmless, which is why only the
+		 * replug path fails. Replugging at an unchanged speed leaves
+		 * the rate adaptation and data path exactly as they were.
+		 */
+		if (!priv->ports[index].speed_changed) {
+			dev_dbg(priv->dev, "link_up: speed unchanged, skipping global reset\n");
+			return;
+		}
+
 		dev_dbg(priv->dev, "link_up: performing global digital reset\n");
 		an7581_pcs_cdr_reset(priv, index, priv->ports[index].interface, false);
 
